# V756 hardware operation budget — 2026-11-05

Exp8838 reads complete measured CPU work from Exp8835 and paid witness operations
from Exp8831 independently. Exp8825 remains the board-boundary authority.
This is a design audit. It performs no model load, training or board command.

Exp8835 measures 90 windows across 30 constructed streams and three modes.
Each window contains 64 queries, eight-query delayed feedback, a fresh-process
restart at32, and a complete feedback tail. Parent clocks include startup,
imports, response serialization, durable writes and child exit. The result
retains each window total and query cost. Total/100 is a future latency
requirement. It is not a speedup prediction.

The paired differences retain their negative estimates and uncertainty.
Read-only mode still computes gradients before deciding whether to commit them.
Its name does not mean that training arithmetic is free. Feature observations,
five primitive checks, prediction normalization, gradient calls, parameter
commits, template admissions and source-derived store saves are separate counts.
Store saves do not supply a measured fsync fraction or byte count.

Exp8831 supplies separately paid lookup, comparison, binding, query-visit and
join-attempt counts for each world, variant and arm. An observed zero join count
is retained. It does not describe the different joins in the causal store.
Variants and modes do not create new independent worlds. Neither constructed
corpus establishes natural-language or hidden-game generalization.

Three-label normalization enumerates all labels exactly. No MCMC call is present
in these execution paths. A symbolic join and dense backpropagation do not become
Ising sampling because an FPGA has a sampler. The small dense head uses 45 float32
parameters, 180 parameter bytes, and three 9-input candidates with four SiLU units.
Its simple forward matrix products need 120 scalar multiplies per decision.
That source count excludes activation, gradient, loss and compiler work.

Disjoint component time, wire bytes, board startup and transfer remain unknown.
No accepted compatible component fraction exists. No Amdahl curve,10x native
benefit or100x hardware benefit follows from operation counts or vendor figures.

